    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with HTTP 409 Conflict. The change follows the existing conventions in the codebase (mirroring the `DuplicateTelephoneException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException` patterns).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`service/CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 A `RuntimeException` thrown when a new owner's city is at capacity, documented as mapping to a 409.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 Added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant and an `assertCityHasCapacity(...)` check invoked for new owners in `saveOwner(...)`. It counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitively, excluding self \u2014 consistent with the existing `generateCustomerCode`/namesake logic) and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50.\n\n3. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 Added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `CityAtCapacityException` returning `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409), consistent with the other duplicate-handler methods.\n\n**Test results:** The build is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to 50, then expects the 51st to be rejected with 409) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.\n\nNote: this is not a git repository, so I made no commit. Let me know if you'd like me to initialize one and commit.",
