    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean, additive, and matches this codebase's established patterns closely.\n\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** sits in the `service` package alongside its siblings `DuplicateTelephoneException` and `DuplicateHouseholdException`, extends `RuntimeException`, and builds its message the same way. Right unit, natural fit.\n- **The exception handler** in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` mirrors the existing 409 handlers exactly (same `detailBuild` call, same `ResponseEntity.status(status).body(detail)` shape, dedicated `ERROR_*` constant, Javadoc in the house style).\n- **`assertCityHasCapacity`** follows the exact idiom already set by `assertTelephoneIsUnique` and `assertHouseholdIsUnique` in the same file: null-guard, `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()` filtering out self by id, then the predicate. Using `findAll().stream()` to count rather than a `countByCityIgnoreCase` repository method would normally be worth flagging, but here it is the deliberate, consistent pattern of every sibling check in this class \u2014 introducing a repository query method for this one check alone would make it the odd one out. Consistency with the surrounding code wins.\n- The `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` constant is package-private `static final` with a clear Javadoc, and the call is correctly gated behind `owner.isNew()` so updates aren't penalized.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this entirely natural.",
